course: dictionary
lesson: 2982
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word duck can be a noun, a bird that swims and says «quack», or a verb, which means to bend down quickly. The clue is in the sentence around it.
explain: «A duck's quack does echo; scientists tested it in a special sound room.» Here a duck is the bird, because it makes a quack. In «Bread fills ducks up without much goodness», the ducks are animals that eat bread, so the bird meaning fits again.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If you read «Duck!» as a warning to bend down quickly, the sentence still makes sense. If you read it as a bird, it does not. Always test before you decide.
fact: Duck can be a noun (a bird with a flat beak and webbed feet) or a verb (to bend down quickly so you are not hit or seen).
fact: A duck has 2 legs, and a baby duck is called a duckling.
fact: In cricket, a duck is a score of zero.
fact: «Peas, oats, sweetcorn and duck food are better than bread» for feeding ducks, and only in small amounts, because bread makes the water dirty and attracts rats.
fact: In «duck-rabbit», the word duck is joined to rabbit with a dash, to describe a picture that can be seen in two ways.
exercise: «A duck's quack does echo; scientists tested it in a special sound room.» What is a duck in this sentence? | A sound room | *A bird that swims and says quack | To bend down quickly | A score of zero in cricket
exercise: Ben shouted, «Duck!» as the ball flew at him. What does duck mean? | A score of zero | A young duck | A bird with webbed feet | *To bend down quickly so you are not hit
exercise: «Bread fills ducks up without much goodness; peas and oats are better, in small amounts.» Why are peas and oats better for ducks? | *They give ducks more goodness and do not make the water dirty | Ducks can only eat them when it rains | They make ducks fly away | They are sweeter than bread
test:
In cricket, the batter was out for a duck. What does duck mean here? | A bird that swims on the pond | To bend down quickly | *A score of zero | A flat beak
«The ducklings followed their mum across the pond.» What is a duckling? | An old bird | The water in the pond | *A young duck | A kind of bread
exam:
Mia counted six ducks on the pond. In this sentence, what kind of word is ducks? | *A noun, the name of birds | A verb, an action | An adjective, a describing word | A full stop
